      "statement": "Item A3 (docs/THEOREM_COVERAGE.md): LCP(R-hat, 0) has only the trivial solution, where R-hat is the shifted unilateral matrix on the normal players. Why it is needed: [SS] Lemma 2.10 runs in the dangerous direction — a NONTRIVIAL solution would give this game stationary epsilon-equilibria and end the counterexample — so what has to be certified is an absence, and complementarity turns it into a finite disjunction over the support of z. One certificate per nonempty support S, refuting `z_S > 0, R-hat[S,S] z_S = 0, R-hat[S^c,S] z_S >= 0` by a pair (y, l) with l >= 0 and the linear forms v = R-hat[S,S]^T y - R-hat[S^c,S]^T l non-negative and of positive sum. The coefficients of the conditions are the payoff entries, so the substitution is a check about this game. Scope: one file per support, and the case table below is what claims the fifteen are all of them. The step from `only the trivial solution` to `no vanishing-stationary family` is [SS] Lemma 2.10, a human theorem, and is part of no certificate. Related but not the same as the simultaneous_quit group: (L8) refutes `M z = 0, z > 0` on the coalition blocks, and A3 refutes that system with the off-support inequalities added, on all supports including the four singletons that (L8) does not reach.",
