      "statement": "Item A4 (docs/THEOREM_COVERAGE.md): the essential-APS outer iteration of Krasikov empties, so there is no sequentially perfect Flesch absorption path and the game has no continuous equilibrium of that class. What carries it here is a depth argument, not a polytope trace: a piece for player i at step k+1 arises only from the constant path (which needs the solo vector r-hat({i}) >= 0) or from the operator applied to a piece of a successor, so with no solo vector non-negative a nonempty iterate at step k forces a path of k edges in the successor graph S_i = {j != i : R-hat[i,j] < 0 and R-hat[j,i] > 0}. The group therefore contains four solo certificates (a negative coordinate of each r-hat({i})), twelve edge certificates (one per ordered pair, fixing the successor graph from the sign of two payoff entries), and one rank function strictly decreasing along every present edge, whose existence is acyclicity and whose maximum plus one is the step from which every iterate is empty. Scope: the case table below is what claims the twelve pairs are all of them; the step from `every iterate is empty` to `no sequentially perfect FAP` is Krasikov Prop. 4.9, a human theorem and part of no certificate; and A4 closes the jump-free regime only together with (L8), the simultaneous_quit group. The aps_trace certificate type was NOT used, because it verifies declared inclusions and final emptiness but not that each polytope is the operator image of its predecessor, which is the entire link to the game.",
